  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The kernel seam divides a face with a runaway triangle count a second time, over its boundary nodes only.\n- The new division is the Delaunay fill of the boundary loop of the face. It adds no node. It keeps each shared edge node as it is.\n- The seam keeps the new division only when `mesh_deviation::measure_within` proves it inside the tolerance. If not, the face keeps the triangles of the planner.\n- The measure of the whole plan runs after that, as before. The guarantee of a machining mesh does not change.\n- A kept division is a note in the mesh report: `face N: divided over its K boundary nodes (...)`.\n- The known-fail marker of the thread flank test is removed. The test runs in the default suite again.\n\nNew files:\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/mesh_redivide.rs`: the selection of the faces, the boundary loop, the checks, the measure.\n- `crates/kernel/src/mesh_redivide_fill.rs`: the polygon fill (ear clipping, then Lawson flips).\n- `crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh_redivide.rs`: the test of the tolerance gate.\n- `docs/decisions/2844-strip-division.md`: the decisions.\n\nA face is divided again only if it has 10 000 planned triangles or more, and 16 or more for each boundary node. A face with a hole, a pole or a period is not divided.\n\n## Cause\n\nsolidcore-tess plans the long, thin helicoid strip isotropically. Our seam (`machining_mesh::planned`) could only pick the chord. The replan at half the chord made the count larger.\n\nOptions 1 and 2 of the issue are changes in `NeoTech/solidcore`. This PR is option 3 of the issue comment of 2026-11-20: the seam replaces the inside division of one face.\n\n## Readings\n\nFour-turn thread flank at 5e-3 mm, debug build:\n\n| Plan | Planner | Boundary division | Measured |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| chord 5e-3 mm | 274192 triangles | 926 triangles | 7.3e-3 mm, not kept |\n| chord 2.5e-3 mm (replan) | 391338 triangles | 1150 triangles | 3.8e-3 mm, kept |\n\nThe test time is 35 s. It was 68 s.\n\n## Tests (pins, mutation results)\n\nPins:\n\n- `a_four_turn_thread_flank_meshes_at_full_fidelity_in_a_bounded_count` (app, `import_step_thread`). Red on unchanged code: `facet count over the bound: 391338 facets for a four-turn strip`. Green with the fix. All its other asserts stay as they were.\n- `a_wide_twisted_face_keeps_the_planner_division` (kernel, `machining_mesh_redivide`).\n- `mesh_redivide::tests::a_face_is_divided_over_its_boundary_nodes_with_the_same_boundary_and_sense` (kernel lib).\n- `mesh_redivide::tests::a_face_that_is_not_a_plain_region_of_its_shared_nodes_is_not_divided` (kernel lib).\n- `mesh_redivide_fill::tests::a_long_strip_is_filled_with_short_sides_across_it` (kernel lib).\n- `mesh_redivide_fill::tests::collinear_runs_and_a_notch_keep_every_boundary_side` (kernel lib).\n- `mesh_redivide_fill::tests::a_polygon_that_cannot_be_filled_is_refused` (kernel lib).\n\nMutations:\n\n| Mutation | Test | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `machining_mesh.rs` from `upstream/main` (no call) | the thread flank pin | red (391338 facets), then green after the restore |\n| the tolerance gate in `redivide` removed | `a_wide_twisted_face_keeps_the_planner_division` | red (`FaceCapped`), then green |\n| the Lawson flips removed | `a_long_strip_is_filled_with_short_sides_across_it` | red (a side 99.75 long), then green |\n| the check of the last ear removed | `a_polygon_that_cannot_be_filled_is_refused` | red, then green |\n\nGate on the final head `48071efd4`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 10 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- These app suites also ran in debug and are green: `contour_whole_step`, `fixture_step_library`, `import_step_closed_shell`, `import_step_corner_blend`, `import_step_curve_guard`, `import_step_doubly_curved`, `import_step_guard`, `import_step_guard_default_cap`, `import_step_open_shell`, `import_step_outward`, `import_step_twisted_flank`, `model_fidelity`, `step_budget`, `step_chord_units`, `step_fidelity`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes did not run. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 246 release steps. A reviewer must run them before this PR is ready.\n- The 14-turn faces of the user's parts (#1602) did not run. Their boundary has about 4000 nodes, under the bound of 8192 vertices of the fill.\n- No face with a hole was divided: the code refuses such a face before the fill.\n- The time of the planner itself does not change. The planner still makes its isotropic division, and the replan at half the chord remains. The speed item of #2780 stays open.\n- solidcore-tess stays at the pinned rev. No dependency changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2918 touches `crates/kernel/src/lib.rs` (the same file, different lines). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2795 touches `crates/app/tests/import_step_thread.rs` (the same file, a different function: `flank_step`). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: A STEP thread flank (a long, thin helical strip) meshes in about 1000 facets, not 391 000; the kernel divides such a face over its edge nodes and keeps the division only when it measures inside the tolerance (#2844).\n\nFixes #2844\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
